Lay-What: An administrator of the operator workspace can set how busy each machine should stay, and which machine takes the next new agent.
Lay-How: Open workspace settings, choose Fleet load, set the low and high percents and the machine order, then save. Reset one field to put that field back to its usual value.
Lay-Why: The target was stored, but there was no screen to read or change it.
Tech-What: WUI workspace settings calls GET and PATCH /v1/operator/fleet-load.
Tech-How: The nav entry is shown only when that GET returns 200. A reset sends JSON null. A 400 bad_setting shows the hub detail text.
Tech-Why: The operator-admin rule is not a session permission row, so the screen asks the hub instead of reading the session.
